OrionLayer open fix 111 — the colony screen's demolish, addressed by id
=======================================================================

Work order 323 ("the building demolish", Data's answer P3 to 321: "Das
Abreissen von Gebaeuden werden wir bauen."). orion2re on the fork's branch
`orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top of open fix 110; commit da87ff51. Not on
`orionlayer-local`. In src/ext/ext_api.cpp, src/ext/ext_api.h,
src/ext/ext_server.cpp, src/ext/ext_server.h, src/game/colony.cpp under
ORION2RE_EXT, and the fork's docs/extension-api.md.

The original demolishes a building on a LEFT click on the colony screen
(the lines are the branch's at 64b570d4, before this fix moved colony.cpp's
by 3 from the top and by 13 after :1908; the comments in the commit cite
the patched tree). A satellite in orbit has its own hidden field
(Add_Satellite_Fields, colony.cpp:1703-1730) and Check_Satellite_Fields
(:1555-1598) asks "scrap it?" on that field alone. A building of the scene
has a hidden field around its centre (Add_Bldg_Fields, :1674-1701, added
before the full-screen field colony_fields[0], colony_main.cpp:992-995),
and Check_Bldg_Fields (colony.cpp:1902-1998) takes either that field or the
full-screen field with the REAL pointer inside the building's polygon
(XY_In_Bldg_Poly, :2041). Its walk over the 36 cells tests, at every cell
before the clicked one, the scanned field (fields::Scan_Input, the field
under the pointer, colony_main.cpp:335) and the pointer's polygon, and
RETURNS there as a mere scan (:1983-1995). So a field activated by id
lands wherever the hidden engine window's pointer is: swallowed, or the
scan of another building. That is why HD could offer nothing (OMISSION
building_actions, work order 180).

What the original then does (colony.cpp:1916-1955): nothing for the
Capitol (its list :1926-1934 also names the Artemis System Net, the
Dimensional Portal, the Star Base, Star Fortress and Battlestation, but
those five are satellites, Satellite_Anim_Pic :193-208 and
colony_main.cpp:539-540, so a click reaches them through
Check_Satellite_Fields, which asks for them like any building); past one building a turn (Can_Scrap_Building,
last_turn_building_destroyed and buildings_scrapped_this_turn against
max_buildings_scrapped_per_turn) the refusal box E 0x243 (GENDRAW::Help);
else the confirmation E 0x107 with the building's name and half its cost
(GENDRAW::Confirmation_Box), and on YES Record_Building_Scrap,
Turn_To_Rubble_CR_Bldg, ERICNET::Remove_Building, COLCALC::Colony_Calculation
and the refund to the treasury. A satellite: the same refusal and the same
confirmation, no exception list, Remove_Satellite_From_Array (:1560-1586).
Both boxes go through TEXTBOX / GENDRAW and reach a client as MSGB (open
fix 29).

The fix: MSG_DEMOLISH (0x8C), int16 colony, int16 building id, and
CAP_DEMOLISH (0x0002) in HELLO_REPLY's capabilities. Taken from the drain loop like MSG_ACTIVATE: only on SCREEN_COLONY, for
COLONY::colony_handle (the player's by construction: the colony screen
sets PLAYER_NUM to its owner, colony_main.cpp:280), outside the planet view (drawing_display 2, in which
Evaluate_Input skips the walk, colony.cpp:1316) and with no activation
waiting, for a building the colony has (buildings[id] != 0). The field is
the one the original would have been clicked on: the satellite slot first,
as Evaluate_Input asks satellites first (:1320-1321), else the first cell
of the walk's own row-major order that holds the building; it is
activated as MSG_ACTIVATE does (g_pending_field). For a cell,
ext::Take_Demolish_Field, called at the top of Check_Bldg_Fields, is true
once for exactly that activation (ext::g_activated_input, fields.cpp:190-
194) and makes the walk read the activated field as the scanned one and
the pointer at (-1000, -1000) — below every polygon (the polygon table's y
runs 288..492) — so no earlier cell claims it. Everything after is the
original's branch, unchanged, its boxes in the colony screen's own loop.
A building with no field is refused, as the original cannot click it: a
station another supersedes (Sat_Should_Be_Replaced, colony.cpp:226-243)
and a building the full grid has no cell for
(Find_Replacement_Slot_For_Building, :260). (colony_main.cpp:538's cap of
18 is the ground-combat view's, is_ui_view 1, not the colony screen's.)

Form (decision 97): a message, not a new field. The fields already exist;
what was missing was a click the pointer cannot redirect, and a message
that names the colony and the building is checked against the screen at
the moment it is taken, where a field index the client read a moment
earlier may already belong to the next colony's scene. One message, one
hook of four lines in the game's code; no structure or logic of the game
changed; addressed by game-level identities (colony index, building id),
so nothing of the engine's layout is frozen; a capability bit and a row in
docs/extension-api.md.

Live: UNVERIFIED — no live run (Data's decision of 20 October 2026); built
and compiled (`linux-debug`, ORION2RE_EXT on) on the scratch clone and in
~/orion2re.

Amended (work order 323's review, commit f6177a05, README row 25fdf420;
its v2 file doc/v2/fix111-amended.patch): refused while anything runs its
own input loop over the colony screen (MSGB - the E 0x243 refusal is a
Help box that keeps the colony's fields, so a DEMOLISH under it dismissed
it -, TPOP, a reported id, a list field, a film) and when the field found
no longer has the rect Add_Bldg_Fields / Add_Satellite_Fields gave it (a
popup that replaced the fields, COLXPORT::Xport_Popup); the arm lives only
while its activation waits and for the pass that took it; the owner test,
a tautology on the colony screen, is gone; the comments corrected as
above.

